"message\">Is there, in any of the three editions, a martial arts style that focuses on long, thrusting</div> </div> </div> </div>Sapphire Veils of Passion!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1042640-madam-i-challenge-you-to-a-duel#post1042640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">swords?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Oh</i>. Uhm. Five Dragon Style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/K9a6Pmp.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","name":"Korhal_IV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"592"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T08:09:15-08:00","id":1042953,"title":"","content":"Lore checks! This is a perfect opportunity for a PC Lore check in the middle of the game. Dueling codes are one of those things you can quickly establish to your favor in one encounter, only for the ST to turn it around and play it against you in a later scene (all in the name of consistency, of course!)<br /> <br /> Of all of Lore's many, many weapons, the double-edged ones are the most fun. One of these days I'm going to get to play a Dawn with Lore 3 (Martial Traditions +1), one of these days...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","name":"Ketrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"398"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T11:25:38-08:00","id":1043058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1042640-madam-i-challenge-you-to-a-duel?p=1042805#post1042805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is totally some nation in Creation where they use an ancient children's card game to resolve arguments.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=j2Y0VqeKxyg\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Behold the ancient and sacred banned card list!&quot;</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T11:35:16-08:00","id":1043062,"title":"","content":"I can't remember where it was (maybe Scroll of the Monk?) but there's an arena in the south that is run by the god Kokage, master of duels.<br /> <br /> There was a custom martial arts style for fancy rapier/smallsword duelling somewhere that I think was called Graceful Hummingbird.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure in Scavenger Sons duelling was mentioned as being an important cultural institution in Calin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T03:14:57-07:00","id":1231546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1042640-madam-i-challenge-you-to-a-duel?p=1043062#post1043062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't remember where it was (maybe Scroll of the Monk?) but there's an arena in the south that is run by the god Kokage, master of duels.<br /> <br /> There was a custom martial arts style for fancy rapier/smallsword duelling somewhere that I think was called Graceful Hummingbird.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty sure in Scavenger Sons duelling was mentioned as being an important cultural institution in Calin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't Graceful Hummingbird one of JiveX's styles?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T04:04:18-07:00","id":1231549,"title":"","content":"The version I remember was credited to Holden.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T04:55:26-07:00","id":1231552,"title":"","content":"If I recall correctly, duelists in Chiaroscuro had many different options to pick from for duels, not just swords and firewands. <br /> <br /> That's right, <i>it's time for a yo-yo duel!</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T05:16:30-07:00","id":1231556,"title":"","content":"Guys.<br /> Dance-off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-01T09:51:21-07:00","id":1231602,"title":"","content":"Anyone who invested in the running charms for Solars would likely freak out over getting to duel via a race.<br /> <br /> A cook-off would be popular in food rich areas, as would a game of riddles or Creation based Jeopardy in a scholarly place.<br /> <br /> From all of 2nd edition's Malfeas bits, i like the idea of the dance-off being something demons excel at. Loke, for such violent and vindictive beings, formal duels are brought to the dance floor.<br /> <br /> Lore or War is likely used for strategic games, but a Liar's Dice game needs max Guile. And I'm sure Larceny would help plenty of card games.<br /> <br /> For levels of seriousness. A contest may help settle issues or arguments, or put some person or group in charge for a period of time (right to rule by duel could be big).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24220-cryo-seraph","name":"Cryo-Seraph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}